      "body": "## Summary\n\nMonetrix treats HyperCore precompile `0x811` as a supply-only balance source, but Hyperliquid's official `L1Read.sol` defines `0x811` as a borrow-lend user-state object containing **both** `borrow` and `supply` values for a token.\n\n`PrecompileReader.suppliedBalance()` decodes the four `uint64` words returned by `0x811` and keeps only the last one. As a result:\n\n- PM-supplied collateral is counted into backing\n- PM borrow liabilities are never subtracted\n\nThis lets `totalBackingSigned()` and `surplus()` become positive even when the true PM net state is negative. Once that happens, `settle()` can admit yield that should have been blocked by Gate 3, and `distributeYield()` can route that unbacked value to stakers / insurance / foundation.\n\n\nHyperliquid's official [`Interacting with HyperCore`](https://hyperliquid.gitbook.io/hyperliquid-docs/for-developers/hyperevm/interacting-with-hypercore) docs ship an attached `L1Read.sol` that defines `0x811` as:\n\n```solidity\nstruct BasisAndValue {\n    uint64 basis;\n    uint64 value;\n}\n\nstruct BorrowLendUserTokenState {\n    BasisAndValue borrow;\n    BasisAndValue supply;\n}\n```\n\nSo the `0x811` payload is not \"supplied amount only.\" It is:\n\n1. `borrow.basis`\n2. `borrow.value`\n3. `supply.basis`\n4. `supply.value`\n\nBut Monetrix reads it like this:\n\n```solidity\nfunction suppliedBalance(address account, uint64 token) internal view returns (uint64 supplied) {\n    (bool ok, bytes memory res) = HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_SUPPLIED_BALANCE.staticcall(\n        abi.encode(account, token)\n    );\n    require(ok && res.length >= 128, \"PrecompileReader: supplied balance read failed\");\n    (,,, supplied) = abi.decode(res, (uint64, uint64, uint64, uint64));\n}\n```\n\nThat drops the entire borrow side by construction.\n\nThen `_readL1Backing()` adds the interpreted supply values:\n\n```solidity\nif (a.spotToken == uint64(HyperCoreConstants.USDC_TOKEN_INDEX)) {\n    total += int256(PrecompileReader.suppliedUsdcEvm(account));\n} else {\n    total += int256(\n        PrecompileReader.suppliedNotionalUsdcFromPerp(uint32(a.spotToken), a.perpIndex, account)\n    );\n}\n```\n\nThere is no corresponding subtraction of `borrow.value`.\n\nThis becomes exploitable in normal PM flows:\n\n1. the Vault supplies collateral under PM, e.g. through `executeHedge()` or `supplyToBlp()`\n2. PM auto-borrow / borrow-lend state creates a negative quote liability\n3. Monetrix counts the supplied collateral through `0x811`\n4. Monetrix does **not** subtract the PM borrow side from the same official precompile state\n5. `surplus()` becomes overstated\n6. `settle()` accepts yield that should have failed the distributable-surplus gate\n7. `distributeYield()` routes real value out based on that phantom surplus\n\nThis is not an offchain monitoring issue. The onchain safety gate itself is reading the borrow-lend state incorrectly.\n\n## Impact\n\nThis breaks the protocol's core backing invariant for PM accounts.\n\nThe concrete sink is false-positive yield settlement:\n\n- the protocol believes backing exceeds liabilities\n- `settleDailyPnL()` therefore accepts a `proposedYield`\n- `settle()` moves real USDC into `YieldEscrow`\n- `distributeYield()` then:\n  - mints fresh `USDM` into `sUSDM` for the user share\n  - routes the insurance share into `InsuranceFund`\n  - routes the foundation share to the foundation\n\nSo a PM borrow that should have reduced backing can instead be ignored while yield is distributed as if the protocol were solvent.\n\nThis is Medium:\n\n- It is an accounting defect in a core value-measurement path\n- It admits value distribution that should have been blocked by the onchain settlement guard\n\n## Recommended Mitigation\n\nDo not treat `0x811` as a supply-only balance source.\n\nMonetrix should decode and account for the full official borrow-lend user state:\n\n- subtract `borrow.value`\n- add `supply.value`\n\nand it should do so for every PM token state that can economically affect backing, not only for the positive supplied side. The settlement guard must be based on the true net PM asset/liability state before any yield is declared.",
      "proofOfConcept": "This PoC demonstrates that:\n\n1. Monetrix counts the `supply.value` half of a USDC `0x811` borrow-lend state into backing while ignoring the `borrow.value` half from that same official precompile payload\n2. that omission can make `surplus()` positive even when the honest net PM state is insolvent\n3. once `surplus()` is falsely positive, `settle()` and `distributeYield()` can route yield that should have been blocked by Gate 3\n\n### Steps to run from a fresh clone\n\n1. Clone and enter the contest repo:\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/code-423n4/2026-04-monetrix.git\ncd 2026-04-monetrix\ngit submodule update --init --recursive\n```\n\n2. Replace only the body of `test_submissionValidity()` in `test/c4/C4Submission.t.sol` with the PoC below.\n3. Run:\n\n```bash\nforge test --match-path \"test/c4/C4Submission.t.sol\" -vvv\n```\n\nExpected result: `test_submissionValidity()` passes and shows that a PM borrow-lend user state with supplied collateral plus borrowed USDC can produce positive `surplus()`, admit `settle()`, and distribute yield even though the honest PM net is negative once `borrow.value` is included.\n\n### Inline PoC\n\n\n```solidity\nfunction test_submissionValidity() public {\n    uint256 totalLiability = 100_000_000e6;\n    uint256 seededStake = 1_000e6;\n    uint256 usdcSuppliedCollateral = 100_200_000e6;\n    uint256 usdcBorrowLiability = 100_150_000e6;\n    uint256 proposedYield = 50_000e6;\n\n    // Seed a tiny live staking cohort so falsely admitted yield is actually routed to users.\n    vm.prank(address(vault));\n    usdm.mint(user1, totalLiability);\n    _stake(user1, seededStake);\n\n    // Register the 0x811 PM user-state slot that the Accountant will query.\n    vm.prank(address(vault));\n    accountant.notifyVaultSupply(uint64(HyperCoreConstants.USDC_TOKEN_INDEX), 0);\n\n    // Hyperliquid 0x811 = BorrowLendUserTokenState {\n    //   borrow { basis, value },\n    //   supply { basis, value }\n    // }\n    // Monetrix only uses the final word, i.e. supply.value, so a positive\n    // USDC supply can be counted while the USDC borrow side is ignored.\n    _PoCMockPrecompile(payable(HyperCoreConstants.PRECOMPILE_SUPPLIED_BALANCE)).setResponse(\n        abi.encode(address(vault), uint64(HyperCoreConstants.USDC_TOKEN_INDEX)),\n        abi.encode(\n            uint64((usdcBorrowLiability - 1e6) * 100),\n            uint64(usdcBorrowLiability * 100),\n            uint64(usdcSuppliedCollateral * 100),\n            uint64(usdcSuppliedCollateral * 100)\n        )\n    );\n\n    assertEq(accountant.totalBackingSigned(), int256(usdcSuppliedCollateral), \"supply side counted\");\n    assertEq(accountant.surplus(), int256(usdcSuppliedCollateral - totalLiability), \"borrow omitted from surplus\");\n\n    int256 honestBacking = int256(usdcSuppliedCollateral) - int256(usdcBorrowLiability);\n    int256 honestSurplus = honestBacking - int256(totalLiability);\n\n    assertLt(honestSurplus, 0, \"real PM state is net insolvent once borrow is included\");\n    assertGt(accountant.surplus(), 0, \"protocol sees phantom positive surplus\");\n\n    usdc.mint(address(vault), proposedYield);\n    vm.warp(block.timestamp + 2 days);\n\n    uint256 annualCap = (usdm.totalSupply() * config.maxAnnualYieldBps() * 2 days) / (10_000 * 365 days);\n    assertGt(annualCap, proposedYield, \"gate 4 does not block chosen yield\");\n\n    vm.startPrank(admin);\n    vault.settle(proposedYield);\n    vault.distributeYield();\n    vm.stopPrank();\n\n    uint256 userShare = (proposedYield * config.userYieldBps()) / 10_000;\n\n    assertEq(susdm.totalAssets(), seededStake + userShare, \"false-positive yield reached live stakers\");\n    assertEq(usdc.balanceOf(address(yieldEscrow)), 0, \"yield escrow fully distributed\");\n    assertEq(accountant.surplus(), int256(usdcSuppliedCollateral - totalLiability), \"phantom surplus survives\");\n    assertLt(honestSurplus, 0, \"honest net state never had distributable surplus\");\n}\n```",
